Adds "reserva técnica" per claude/plan-comparacion-ozmap.md backlog
item #1: extra cable coiled at each end of a route for splicing/
rework room. Matches OZmap's documented rule that reserve is counted
at BOTH ends (a 15ft value adds 30ft total) — feeds directly into
installed_length_feet, which already drives the BOM's linear-footage
lines and the mirrored conduit_runs length, so the reserve now flows
through to material quantities automatically.

- migration: fiber_routes.technical_reserve_ft numeric default 15
- actions-fiber.ts: createFiberRoute/updateFiberRoute accept
  technicalReserveFt, apply it x2 in the installed-length formula
- FiberMapCanvas.tsx: new "Technical Reserve (ft/end)" field next to
  Slack Loop (%) on the route detail panel, with a note showing the
  doubled total
- src/types/supabase.ts: hand-patched the fiber_routes Row/Insert/
  Update types with the new column (full `generate_typescript_types`
  regen was dropped — it omitted the still-live organization_branding
  table, so it was discarded rather than used)

